  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145838",
      "title": "Using Server-side Rendering (SSR)",
      "lectureOrder": 299,
      "videoOrder": 278,
      "sourceHash": "5a38e0151b7ce30e72eab724207989649ba63c5237357464dafb1848c83bf05d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 6.55,
          "en": "So here on this slug page, on this catch all page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.55,
          "end": 10.82,
          "en": "we're currently getting the concrete path values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.82,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "from the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 14.83,
          "en": "to then get the year and the month",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.83,
          "end": 19.57,
          "en": "and fetch the appropriate events for us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.57,
          "end": 23.45,
          "en": "Now the question is, how do we wanna do that in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.45,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "with our newly gained knowledge?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "And we have a couple of options here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "We can use getStaticProps to pre-generate this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 35.47,
          "en": "But of course, for the filtered events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.47,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "we'll have a lot of different combinations of parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 44.21,
          "en": "2021, and one, and five, and two, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.29,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "That's not necessarily an issue, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.99,
          "en": "because we will have to use getStaticPaths anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.99,
          "end": 54.85,
          "en": "and once we add that, we could only pre-render a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.85,
          "end": 58.07,
          "en": "of those combinations, and not all of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.07,
          "end": 63.02,
          "en": "And instead, then, use fallback set to true or blocking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.02,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "But how should we decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 67.51,
          "en": "which paths should be pre-generated?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.51,
          "end": 72.02,
          "en": "In the end, all possible filters are equally likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.02,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "to be visited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 76.78999999999999,
          "en": "So, I would have a hard time picking a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.78999999999999,
          "end": 80.36,
          "en": "of combinations that should be pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.36,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "And pre-generating all possible combinations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 85.43,
          "en": "is also not a great option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.43,
          "end": 87.86,
          "en": "because that could be a lot of pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.86,
          "end": 90.963,
          "en": "Especially if we have no year restriction, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 96.19,
          "en": "So, getStaticProps might not be ideal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.19,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "Maybe, here, getServerSideProps is better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 104.12,
          "en": "So that we do indeed fetch the data on the fly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.12,
          "end": 107.83,
          "en": "for every incoming request, and we then return the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.83,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 112.15,
          "en": "So let's start with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.15,
          "end": 117.15,
          "en": "In this slug page, I will export an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.07,
          "end": 122.267,
          "en": "called getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.4,
          "end": 127.41,
          "en": "You know that here we get the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.41,
          "end": 129.55,
          "en": "And then here we wanna return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.55,
          "end": 133.81,
          "en": "which is similar to the object we return in getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.81,
          "end": 137.93,
          "en": "With the props key and possibly also with the not found key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.93,
          "end": 139.773,
          "en": "and the redirect key if we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.11,
          "end": 146.11,
          "en": "Now here, from the context, we can get access to the params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "So here, we can get access to the parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 152.62,
          "en": "for which this page was visited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.62,
          "end": 154.38,
          "en": "And that's good because now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 157.76,
          "en": "we basically wanna repeat what we previously did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.76,
          "end": 160.03,
          "en": "in our component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.03,
          "end": 163.54,
          "en": "We wanna get our year and month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.54,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "and convert that to a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 167.82,
          "en": "and then validate it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.82,
          "end": 171.173,
          "en": "and then ultimately get our filtered events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.44,
          "en": "So I will copy all that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.44,
          "end": 176.42000000000002,
          "en": "though we're going to edit it a bit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.42000000000002,
          "end": 178.46,
          "en": "but I'll copy all that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.46,
          "end": 180.883,
          "en": "and bring it down there into getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.67,
          "end": 186.18,
          "en": "Now here, we're accessing filtered data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.18,
          "end": 188.48,
          "en": "that should actually be our params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.48,
          "end": 192.45,
          "en": "Because up there, filtered data is also just what we read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.45,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "from the router query, which are also our params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "when accessed through useRouter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 202.447,
          "en": "So therefore here I'll rebuild filterData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.59,
          "end": 206.07,
          "en": "and access params.slug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 207.79,
          "en": "So we still access .slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.79,
          "end": 212.34,
          "en": "because that is our catch-all grouping parameter name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.34,
          "end": 214.42000000000002,
          "en": "if you wanna call it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.42000000000002,
          "end": 218.29,
          "en": "And that will still be an array with multiple values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.29,
          "end": 221.17000000000002,
          "en": "and we are interested in the first two values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.17000000000002,
          "end": 223.76,
          "en": "which should be the year and the month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.76,
          "end": 225.7,
          "en": "Which is why we convert them to numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.7,
          "end": 228.44,
          "en": "and then validate them down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.44,
          "end": 232.81,
          "en": "Now if validation fails, however, we don't wanna return JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.81,
          "end": 235.043,
          "en": "That's not possible in getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "We always have to return an object instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 241.39,
          "en": "But if the validation fails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.39,
          "end": 245.72,
          "en": "I don't wanna return a props object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.72,
          "end": 247.39,
          "en": "or a props key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.39,
          "end": 250.92,
          "en": "Instead, here, I'll then set notFound to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.92,
          "end": 253.37,
          "en": "I wanna show the 404 page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.37,
          "end": 257.223,
          "en": "if an invalid parameter combination is passed in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.35,
          "end": 263.33,
          "en": "We could also consider redirecting to some error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.33,
          "end": 264.95,
          "en": "if we had one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.95,
          "end": 266.58,
          "en": "But here, we don't have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.58,
          "end": 268.85,
          "en": "We could add one, but I will not do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.85,
          "end": 270.08,
          "en": "So I'll comment this out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.08,
          "end": 273.827,
          "en": "and instead show the 404 error page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.827,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "Another alternative would be to set some props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 279.81,
          "en": "like the hasError prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.81,
          "end": 282.2,
          "en": "and then handle this specific prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.2,
          "end": 286.77,
          "en": "in our component function to show an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.77,
          "end": 287.603,
          "en": "And actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.603,
          "end": 291.14,
          "en": "since we do have that error specific JSX code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.14,
          "end": 294.06,
          "en": "that might actually be the best alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.06,
          "end": 296.45,
          "en": "So it's still worth knowing the other ones,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.45,
          "end": 298.99,
          "en": "but I will now not show the 404 page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.99,
          "end": 302.07,
          "en": "but instead return my special hasError prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.07,
          "end": 305.253,
          "en": "set to true if the validation fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.25,
          "end": 308.52,
          "en": "So that in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.52,
          "end": 311.13,
          "en": "in this FilteredEventsPage function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.13,
          "end": 314.92,
          "en": "we should expect props, and then down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.92,
          "end": 318.49,
          "en": "instead of validating our query parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318.49,
          "end": 322.34,
          "en": "I check if props hasError is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.34,
          "end": 325.723,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I'll show this error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.58,
          "end": 329.2,
          "en": "I think that actually makes the most sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 329.2,
          "end": 330.36,
          "en": "but you can also go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.36,
          "end": 332.593,
          "en": "with one of the two alternatives I showed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.25,
          "end": 337.44,
          "en": "Now if we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.44,
          "end": 340.68,
          "en": "we do have valid parameter values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.68,
          "end": 344.40999999999997,
          "en": "and therefore now we wanna get our filtered events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.40999999999997,
          "end": 347.07,
          "en": "For this, I'll go to dummy data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.07,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "and take this getFilteredEvents function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 354.73,
          "en": "and bring that over into api-util.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 354.73,
          "end": 355.803,
          "en": "Maybe down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.99,
          "end": 361.59,
          "en": "Here, we getFilteredEvents by reaching out to DUMMY_EVENTS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.59,
          "end": 363.67,
          "en": "and calling filter on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 363.67,
          "end": 366,
          "en": "Now just as in the other functions here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 366,
          "end": 369.75,
          "en": "I will instead now turn this into a async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.75,
          "end": 373.173,
          "en": "then get access to allEvents by awaiting getAllEvents,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.084,
          "end": 376.76,
          "en": "and then using allEvents here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.76,
          "end": 379.463,
          "en": "instead of DUMMY_EVENTS for filtering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 381.86,
          "end": 385.1,
          "en": "And with that, back in this slug page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 385.1,
          "end": 388.04,
          "en": "we now wanna import getFilteredEvents,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 388.04,
          "end": 391.85,
          "en": "not from dummy-data, but from the helpers folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 391.85,
          "end": 395.15999999999997,
          "en": "and the api-util file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 395.15999999999997,
          "end": 398.277,
          "en": "And then down there in getServerSideProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.22,
          "end": 401.90999999999997,
          "en": "we now get our filtered events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 401.90999999999997,
          "end": 404.63,
          "en": "by awaiting getFilteredEvents,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.63,
          "end": 408,
          "en": "to which we still pass this object with this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408,
          "end": 411.22,
          "en": "Because I haven't changed the function's signature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.22,
          "end": 412.31,
          "en": "of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.31,
          "end": 414.403,
          "en": "It still wants the same parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 415.53,
          "end": 418.39,
          "en": "But we should await because this is now an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 418.39,
          "end": 420.133,
          "en": "returning a promise, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 421.16,
          "end": 423.34,
          "en": "So that gives us our filteredEvents,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 423.34,
          "end": 427.67,
          "en": "and hence, here, through props, we can expose our events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 427.67,
          "end": 428.91,
